// uefi-fs: the system table, boot services, Block I/O and Simple File System
// on the USB floppy, GOP and the console (milestone 3 of fw/README.md). The
// boot manager falls through to the built-in EFI shell, which runs
// uefi-fs.nsh from the fw_cfg volume as startup.nsh: it lists MikeOS's
// floppy (FAT12, fs0:), prints a file from it, starts the GOP (the console
// carries on in pixels) and powers off through ResetSystem.
// requires: ${WORK}/mikeos.flp
// vsim-args: -b test -M 128 -U ${WORK}/mikeos.flp,ro -f opt/vibe86/fs/startup.nsh=${DATA}/uefi-fs.nsh -H 1000000000 -c 400000000
// expect-exit: 0   (powered off by "reset -s")
// expect-out: fs0: Alias(s): vibe86 USB Floppy
// expect-out: fs1: Alias(s): QEMU fw_cfg volume
// expect-out: Directory of: fs0:\
// expect-out: kernel.bin
// expect-out: REM ADVENTURE 2.3 -- By Justin Tokarchuk
// expect-out: gop: 2 modes; not started (the display is in text mode)
// expect-out: *0: 640x480, format 1, 640 pixels per line
// expect-out: frame buffer f0000000, 1228800 bytes
// expect-out: ACPI_NVS
